A maniacal and impulsive criminal from Zaun, Jinx lives to wreak havoc without stopping to think about the consequences. With an arsenal of lethal... Jinx has a volatile personality, trying to suppress his past and prove that he is not weak. He stands out for his chaotic and playful way of being.
Jinx's manic personality is born in a different way. He is born out of pain, confusion, loss and the feeling of abandonment and betrayal, guilt. Jinx loses everything, his friends, his sister and his childhood friend; Tomie.

Looking at Jinx, most just see an insane man with a wide variety of dangerous weapons; Yet few remember her as the relatively innocent child of Zaun, an inventor with great ideas that he was never quite a fit for. No one knows for sure what happened to turn that sweet boy into a wild and unpredictable man, infamous for his senseless acts of destruction. But once Jinx burst onto the Piltover scene, his unique talent for wreaking lawlessness made him a legend.
Jinx first came to attention through his anonymous "pranks" against the citizens of Piltover, especially those associated with wealthy trading clans. These pranks ranged from mildly annoying to criminally dangerous. He blocked the streets on Progress Day with a stampede of exotic animals that he pulled from Earl Mei's collection. He disrupted commerce for weeks when he adorned the city's iconic bridges with adorably destructive fire chewers. On one occasion, he even managed to relocate all the signs in the city to completely new and confusing places.
Despite the fact that the objectives of this unknown troublemaker seemed random, with a motivation rooted exclusively in pure chaos, her actions were always aimed at curbing the orderly bustle of the city.
Naturally, the Protectors attributed some of her crimes to the chemopunk gangs of the suburban district. Jinx didn't like others taking credit for her maniacal plans, so she made sure to publicize her presence at every crime scene. Soon, rumors began to circulate about the mysterious blue-haired Zaunite boy carrying techno-chemical explosives, a shark-shaped rocket launcher, and a machine gun. Even so, the authorities considered these reports ridiculous and dismissed them. After all, how could a street punk get that lethal ammunition?
Jinx's spree of bombastic crimes seemed endless, as the Protectors' attempts to catch the culprit were thwarted all the time. He began tagging his destruction jobs with animated graffiti and other taunting messages directed at the town sheriff's new crime-fighting ally: vigilante Vi.
Jinx's reputation grew to such an extent that opinions of her among the inhabitants of Zaun were divided: some considered her a hero for turning on the arrogant scoundrels, while others saw her as nothing more than a dangerous lunatic who would further fuel the wars. tensions between them. the two cities
After months of relentless carnage, Jinx revealed her biggest plan yet. In her signature electric pink color, Jinx defaced the walls of the Ecliptic Vaults, one of Piltover's most secure treasures, with an unflattering caricature of the vigilante Vi, along with details of how she planned to steal what was stored there.
An eerie sense of anticipation settled in Piltover and Zaun in the days leading up to the promised date of the great coup. Many doubted that Jinx had the guts to come forward and risk almost certain capture.
When the day came, Vi, Sheriff Caitlyn, and the Protectors set Jinx up outside the treasury. But Jinx had already slipped inside through a large coin box that she had given him a few days ago. When Vi heard the chaos erupting from inside the building, she knew that the Protectors had been outmatched again. He abruptly entered the treasury. The ensuing confrontation reduced the Ecliptic Vaults to burning ruins, while the cheerful troublemaker Jinx was nowhere to be seen.
Jinx is still on the run to this day and is a constant nuisance to Piltover. Her actions have inspired crimes that try to imitate her style among chemopunks, as well as numerous satirical representations that parody the incompetence of the Protectors and even some new colloquialisms between the two cities, although no one has yet dared to call it "Manototas". in front of Watcher Vi.
Both Jinx's ultimate goal and his clear obsession with Vi remain a mystery, but one thing is for sure: his crimes persist and grow ever more daring.
